# Comment Contract

Prefer richer comments **where they preserve intent** agents and humans would otherwise lose (signing rules, feed edge cases).

## Add comments when code is non-obvious

Prefer comments around:

- signing / canonicalization / merge invariants (`signing.ts`, merge helpers)
- PATCH vs POST semantics and why refetch matters before merge
- extension policy overrides (`Dp1ExtensionsContext`, env fallbacks)
- URI validation philosophy (prod vs debug)
- any intentional divergence from [dp1-feed-v2](https://github.com/display-protocol/dp1-feed-v2) observable behavior

## Good comment content

Comments should preserve:

- why the code exists
- invariants it must preserve
- failure modes and degraded UX expectations
- design trade-offs
- unresolved owner-level decisions affecting later changes

## Avoid low-value comments

Do not narrate obvious JSX structure, trivial hooks, or what the next line mechanically does.
